---
title: Curried shallot tart
servings: 4
yield: 4 tarts
tags: [vegetarian]
source: Curried Shallot Tart by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/curried-shallot-tart
---

== Roasted curried shallots ==

Toss the @shallots{10}(peeled, halved lengthwise) with the @olive oil{1%cup}, @curry powder{2%tbsp}, the juice and zest of @lemons{2}, @honey{1%tbsp} and the leaves from @thyme{4%sprigs}.

Heat a #large sauté pan{} over medium-high heat. Sear the shallots cut side down ~{5%minutes}, until deeply caramelized. Move them to a bowl.

== Glaze ==

Whisk more @honey{}, the juice and zest of @lemons{2} and the leaves from @thyme{4%sprigs}. Toss the shallots in it and let cool.

== Tarts ==

Heat the oven to 350°F. Roll the @puff pastry{1%sheet} on a lightly floured counter and cut it into squares.

Beat the @egg{1} with @water{2%tbsp}.

On a #half sheet pan{} lined with parchment, arrange the shallots seared side down in clusters about 1/2 inch smaller than the squares, 2 inches apart. Lay a pastry square over each, press the edges down around them and score the tops.

Brush with the egg wash and finish with @sea salt{}, @thyme{}(sprigs) and a pinch of @curry powder{}.

Bake ~{12%minutes}, until golden. Let cool, then flip over to serve.
